> Original MNIST, statically thresholded at byte128

Native preparation acquires checked original MNIST and creates disjoint balanced pools of
1,000 fitting,200 validation and200 official test images. LoadSaliency checks geometry,
byte range, labels, unique pixels, split IDs and100/20/20 observations per digit. Fitting and
validation IDs are from0–59,999; official test IDs are offset into60,000–69,999. Provenance
and the independent seeded row selection are retained in manifest.json. Normalized Float32
pixels are thresholded at0.5, equivalent to original byte≥128. Both originals and binary pixels
are saved, with their labels and source IDs. This is static thresholding, not the official
binarized-MNIST benchmark or random per-epoch Bernoulli binarization.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build/cvae");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  n::NamedTensors saved;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    const auto&       d     = pools[k];
    saved.emplace_back(split + "_original_images", d.images);
    saved.emplace_back(
        split + "_images", n::cast(n::greater_equal(d.images, .5), n::DType::Float32));
    saved.emplace_back(split + "_source_ids", d.source);
    saved.emplace_back(split + "_labels", d.labels);
  }
  n::save_npz("build/cvae/data.npz", saved);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency/manifest.json",
      "build/cvae/data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print(
      "| split | binary images | each supplied digit "
      "|\n|---|---:|---:|\n|fit|1000|100|\n|validation|200|20|\n|official test|200|20|\n");
}
