> Heldout results and reconstruction controls

The selected epoch3 test reconstruction NLL is187.190332 nats/image, KL6.617313 and
negative ELBO193.807644. Decode(mu) MSE is0.076372894; decoding that **same mu** with
class(c+1) mod10 worsens it to0.081708886. Changing the supplied class also changes the
posterior mean (max0.421315), so conditioning is not confined to the decoder. At the same
prior code, changing only the class changes probabilities by up to0.239766. These differences
demonstrate active condition paths, not that every generated image is recognizable.

The fit-global and fit-class means are estimated from binary fitting pixels only. Class means
use100 observations per class and the same supplied test label as the conditional decoder;
this is an appropriate condition-aware baseline rather than a label prediction task. The
global mean MSE is0.086689513, while the fitting class mean MSE is0.071591939: the
class mean outperforms this short-trained model. Decode(mu) is not the posterior predictive
mean. Four sampled outputs per split are saved separately; sigmoid outputs are probabilities,
not Bernoulli pixel samples. Loss values alone do not establish likelihood superiority,
disentanglement, preserved identity or compression bitrate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cvae_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/cvae/history.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> epochs, nll, kl, objective;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    std::istringstream r(line);
    double             e, train, a, b, c;
    r >> e >> train >> a >> b >> c;
    epochs.push_back(e);
    nll.push_back(a);
    kl.push_back(b);
    objective.push_back(c);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(epochs, nll, "NLL", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(epochs, objective, "NLL + KL", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Four fixed posterior draws / completed epochs only")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/cvae_learning.svg");
}
