> Canonical API and reproducible evidence

models::ConditionalVariationalAutoencoder and ConditionalVaeDecode provide reusable native
forwards; the owning ConditionalVaeOutput includes condition, encoder_input and decoder_input
alongside Gaussian endpoints and losses. GaussianReparameterize, DiagonalGaussianKl and
BernoulliPixelNll supply the shared mathematics. Python/R bindings call these same operations;
this report's complete C++ training loop owns all96 updates and validation selection.

Every array of all18 original archives, exact batch TSV and complete validation history is
compared with the saved source run. Evidence includes initial/first-update/all-epoch/selected
weights, all102,932 first derivatives, original and binary data, explicit noise banks, all
posterior samples, standalone decoder controls, condition concatenations, class means and
unfiltered prior/grid probabilities. Independent NumPy checks the chain rule and complete
forward outputs. Repeated fixed noise, epsilon-zero means, changed-noise behavior, invalid
labels, restored checkpoint parity, single/batch agreement and immutable inference execute
inside the report. Numerical checks support this finite run; they do not establish convergence
or make the supplied class into a predicted label.
